---
// Privacy Policy Page
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | TechPulse"
  description="TechPulse privacy policy. Learn how we collect, use, and protect your data."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 19, 2026</p>

    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>Our website address is: <a href="https://willnapolini-bio.github.io/tech-blog/">willnapolini-bio.github.io/tech-blog</a>. TechPulse is an independent tech blog focused on web development tutorials, framework comparisons, and deployment guides.</p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <h3>Automatically Collected Information</h3>
    <p>When you visit our site, we may automatically collect certain information about your device, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Browser type and version</li>
      <li>Operating system</li>
      <li>Referring/exit pages and URLs</li>
      <li>Date and time of visit</li>
      <li>Pages viewed and time spent on pages</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This information is collected through cookies and similar technologies and is used to analyze site traffic and improve your experience.</p>

    <h3>Personally Provided Information</h3>
    <p>If you subscribe to our newsletter, we collect your email address. This information is only used to send you the newsletter content you requested. We do not sell or share your email address with third parties.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use cookies for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Essential cookies:</strong> Required for the site to function properly (e.g., remembering your sponsorship banner dismissal preference via sessionStorage).</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> Help us understand how visitors interact with our site (if analytics are enabled in the future).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can control cookie settings through your browser preferences. Disabling cookies may affect site functionality.</p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <h3>Google Fonts</h3>
    <p>We load fonts from Google Fonts, which may log standard web request information. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h3>GitHub Pages</h3>
    <p>Our site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may collect usage data. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/github/site-policy/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

    <h3>Advertising and Affiliate Networks</h3>
    <p>We may use third-party advertising services (such as Google AdSense or Carbon Ads) that use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits. You can opt out of personalized advertising through <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>

    <h2>Affiliate Links</h2>
    <p>Some links on our site are affiliate links. If you make a purchase through these links, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. These links do not track your personal data beyond standard click-through tracking provided by the affiliate program. See our <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}disclosure`}>Affiliate Disclosure</a> for full details.</p>

    <h2>Data Security</h2>
    <p>We implement reasonable security measures to protect your information. However, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
      <li>Opt out of any newsletter communications</li>
      <li>Disable cookies through your browser settings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about this privacy policy, please contact us through our GitHub repository.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
